---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
// import NavMobile from "../components/NavMobile.astro";
---

<Layout>
	<!-- <Nav /> -->

	<div class="coreContainer animateBG animate image-bg page about">
		<main class="main">
			<article class="bio">
				<div class="bio-content">
					<h1>Meet Jesus Acosta</h1>

					<picture class="bio-pic">
						<img src="/images/sergio.jpg" alt="Sergio Acosta" />
					</picture>
					<p>
						Coding or making art, it all starts with curiosity and a desire for
						understanding and capturing the meaning of things. Making sense of what
						happens. That experience. That event. And then give way to the actual
						crafting of a story, bit by bit.
					</p>
					<p>
						As a developer, I go through this process of investigation using computer
						languages and design principles. It's HTML, JavaScript, CSS, and sometimes,
						modern frameworks like Astro or React.
					</p>
					<p>
						For decades, <a href="/cv/" title="CV"
							>I've been helping corporations as well as small businesses</a
						> at creating dynamic interfaces, keeping clean basecodes and making sure that
						essential messages are transmitted to intended audiences.
					</p>
					<p>
						I also play with my own projects, <a
							href="https://www.danceinconversation.co.uk"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noreferrer"
							title="Dance in Conversation">building up platforms</a
						>
						to share insights and trying to make a positive impact in various corners of
						the web.
					</p>
					<p>
						Welcome to <a href="/"><strong>Designing Stories</strong></a>.
					</p>
				</div>
			</article>
			<!-- <NavMobile /> -->
		</main>
	</div>
</Layout>
